  "notes": "SLANG/TREND:\nタピる was popularized during the ⟦タピオカ→タピオカ：05604_tapioka⟧⟦ブーム→ブーム：05511_buumu⟧ (bubble tea boom) in Japan around 2018-2019. It's a playful verb formed from ⟦タピオカ→タピオカ：05604_tapioka⟧ (tapioca).\n\nFORMS:\n- ⟦タピオカ→タピオカ：05604_tapioka⟧ (tapioca) → タピ (abbreviation) + る (verb ending)\n- Similar pattern: ググる (to google), バズる (to go viral)\n\nCONJUGATION (godan る-verb):\n- タピる (dictionary)\n- タピった (past)\n- タピ⟦って→って：29146_tte⟧ (te-form)\n- タピらない (negative)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦タピオカ→タピオカ：05604_tapioka⟧ - tapioca pearls\n- ⟦タピオカ→タピオカ：05604_tapioka⟧⟦ミルクティー→ミルクティー：27418_mirukutii⟧ - bubble milk tea\n- タピ{活|かつ} - bubble tea activities (trying different shops)\n\nUSAGE:\nMainly used by young people. May sound dated as the bubble tea trend has passed its peak.",
